## Two states you asked me to name

- **Lookup table:** at my first read and first build it was `{}` — `MODE_COMMANDS … = {}`. It was filled *concurrently*, at 15:19:30 UTC, by something outside this brief (`lib/command-attach.ts` plus `scripts/command-bridges/*` have that mtime; I wrote none of them). It now maps `sk-doc → sk-create-readme → /create:readme` (plus `sk-design`, `system-deep-loop`). So `command` was `null` on my first CLI run and `/create:readme` after the rebuild — the code was never the reason for the first `null`.
- **Daemon:** not older code. The serving daemon is pid 42885, lease `startedAt` 15:19:40 UTC, entrypoint mtime 15:19:37 UTC → `predatesBuild: false`, i.e. the CLI's stale-daemon recycle replaced the pre-build daemon before answering. (`liveDaemonPredatesBuild`, `skill-advisor-cli.ts`.)

